scripts/agent-*.bat
scripts/agent-*.json
scripts/mcp-config-*.json
scripts/run-mcp-multiagent-test.bat

# Python bytecode (integrations/*-memory plugins)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.write-secret.tmp
.interego/

# Local agent scratch (patches, split helpers) — per-machine, not source.
.claude/

# Holodeck example state — wallets, MCP configs, run history (operator-local, secret).
.holodeck/
examples/holodeck/.holodeck/

# Editor backups + per-run example artifacts (regenerated each run).
*.bak
examples/tic-tac-toe-tournament/_server.log
examples/tic-tac-toe-tournament/_tournament.log
examples/tic-tac-toe-tournament/last-run.json
# The Azure→Railway migrator stays untracked (it is a one-shot, local, guarded script
# carrying machine-specific paths), but its manifest does NOT.
#
# ★ services.json used to be ignored along with it, and that made a warning unmaintainable.
# The file is a frozen 2026-07-11 snapshot, it is repeatedly misread as a table of what
# production runs, and the `_STALE` banner explaining that was corrected twice — both times
# in a working tree, both times uncommittable, so both times the correction was lost and the
# next reader met the same wrong text. A warning that cannot be committed is not a warning.
#
# `deploy/railway/*` rather than `deploy/railway/`: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory itself must stay un-excluded for the
# negation below to have any effect. Written as `deploy/railway/` the `!` line silently
# does nothing.
deploy/railway/*
!deploy/railway/services.json

# ★ Agent working material: probes, mutation scripts, captured run logs. Never tracked —
# `git ls-tree HEAD scratchpad` is empty across the whole history — but it was never
# IGNORED either, so it showed up as untracked noise in every `git status` and made
# `git add -A` unsafe. Rounds therefore staged from remembered path lists instead, and one
# of them shipped green-locally / red-in-CI by forgetting a file that way. Ignoring it is
# what makes "stage everything you changed" the safe instruction it should always have been.
scratchpad/

# ★ electron-builder output. ~200 MB per target (a bundled Chromium is in each one), produced
# by `npm run package --workspace @interego/workspace-desktop`. `dist/` above already covers the
# bundled entry points; this is the packaged app around them.
applications/shared-workspace/desktop/release/
